WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:15.018
Hi! How many centimetres is 3 m 45 cm? How many kilograms and grams is 4060 g? Today we'll convert between compound units and single units.

2
00:00:15.168 --> 00:00:19.578
First recall: 1 metre is 100 centimetres.

3
00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:25.146
3 metres is 3 hundreds of centimetres, which is 300 cm.

4
00:00:25.296 --> 00:00:32.778
Add 45 cm: 3 m 45 cm is 345 cm.

5
00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:43.626
What about 2 litres 5 millilitres? 2 litres is 2000 ml, plus 5 ml makes 2005 ml.

6
00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:48.186
How many kilograms and grams is 4060 g?

7
00:00:48.336 --> 00:00:55.338
1000 g is 1 kg. 4060 has 4 thousands, so that's 4 kg.

8
00:00:55.488 --> 00:01:01.770
There are 60 g left, so 4060 g is 4 kg 60 g.

9
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:12.618
612 cm has 6 hundreds, which is 6 m, with 12 cm left. So it's 6 m 12 cm.

10
00:01:12.768 --> 00:01:20.562
Watch out! Some pupils write 2 litres 5 millilitres as 25 ml. That's wrong!

11
00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:29.658
We can't just join the numbers. 2 litres is 2000 ml, plus 5 ml makes 2005 ml.

12
00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:36.522
Check afterwards: when you change to a smaller unit, the number gets much bigger.

13
00:01:36.672 --> 00:01:46.098
Your turn! How many centimetres is 1 m 8 cm? Pause and think.

14
00:01:46.248 --> 00:01:55.698
1 m is 100 cm. Add 8 cm: 108 cm. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:55.848 --> 00:02:05.130
Another one! How many metres is 5 km 40 m? Pause and think.

16
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:14.418
5 km is 5000 m. Add 40 m: 5040 m. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:14.568 --> 00:02:25.530
Here's another! How many litres and millilitres is 2350 ml? Pause and think.

18
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:38.082
There are 2 thousands of millilitres, which is 2 litres, with 350 ml left. So 2 litres 350 ml. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:38.232 --> 00:02:47.538
Try one more! How many grams is 3 kg 9 g? Pause and think.

20
00:02:47.688 --> 00:02:56.802
3 kg is 3000 g. Add 9 g: 3009 g. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:56.952 --> 00:03:08.298
Last one! Which is longer, 250 cm or 2 m 45 cm? Pause and think.

22
00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:19.218
2 m 45 cm is 245 cm, so 250 cm is longer. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:19.368 --> 00:03:28.986
Remember: to change a compound unit to one unit, convert the big unit and add. To go the other way, see how many thousands or hundreds there are.

24
00:03:29.136 --> 00:03:34.218
Measure your height and say it in metres and centimetres!

